@notice Lock unminted EWB minting rights as collateral
@dev This is the foundation of the leverage system.
     Wayne locks token IDs that DO NOT EXIST YET on-chain.
     No NFT transfer occurs. The rights are purely on-chain
     proof of Wayne's ability to mint those future tokens.
     Face value is calculated from immutable tier floor constants:
       EPIC:        315 ETH per token
       SUPER RARE:   22 ETH per token
       RARE:         10 ETH per token
       STANDARD:      1 ETH per token
     The resulting lockId is used by EWBMintingRightsVault
     to borrow Circle USDC from Aave against face value × LTV.
@param tokenIds  Unminted EWB token IDs to commit (max 500 per call)
@param purpose   "credit" | "harvest" | "yield"
@param expiresAt Unix timestamp for lock expiry (0 = no expiry)

@notice Release locked minting rights
@dev Only callable by Ballet wallet.
     Should only be called after Aave debt fully repaid.
     Cycle resets — same token IDs can be locked again.

@title EWBKYC
@notice Pure KYC attestation hashing + signature recovery for
        EWBMintingRightsVault. Extracted to reduce parent bytecode.
@dev    Behavior-preserving: identical data hash domain string, identical
        ecrecover handling, identical revert semantics to the original
        inlined code. No storage — all functions are pure.

@title ReentrantERC20
@notice Malicious ERC20 that attempts reentrancy on transfer
@dev Used to verify nonReentrant guards are correctly placed

@notice Pause / unpause all user-facing entrypoints.
         Exempt from timelock — must be instant for incident response.
         Does NOT move funds. Emits event for off-chain monitoring.

@notice Register EWBRevenueRouter for automatic yield recording.
@dev    Once set, harvestYield() notifies the router after each harvest
        so income is tracked on-chain without a separate manual call.
        Safe multisig only. Can be updated if router is redeployed.

@notice Harvest stETH yield — PERMISSIONLESS
@dev Anyone can trigger harvest when yield >= threshold
     Removes owner gate — cannot be blocked by compromised key
     Yield always routes to safeMultisig — cannot be redirected

@notice Stage 0 — Initiate emergency exit
@dev Pauses all operations. Sets EXIT_IN_PROGRESS.
     Call this first then execute stages in order.

@notice Stage 1 — Withdraw wstETH from Aave v3
@dev Idempotent — safe to retry if gas fails
     If Aave is paused, call setAavePaused(true) and wait

@notice Force advance a stuck exit stage
@dev Only callable after EXIT_STAGE_TIMEOUT has elapsed
     Owner must manually handle the stuck stage off-chain

@notice Maximum time per emergency exit stage before forceAdvanceExit() can be called.
         6 hours gives sufficient time for Aave withdrawal + wstETH unwrap under normal conditions.
         If a stage hangs (Aave paused, Curve pool drained), coldWallet can force-advance after 6h.
